{"v":1,"agent":"claude-code","cli_version":"dev","type":"assistant","ts":"2026-07-03T20:26:59.069Z","id":"msg_01634HQ7RohyCM9ZCjvUppN8","input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1374,"content":[{"text":"I dug into what each of those files actually is, and I want to flag something before writing anything: **spreading the ticket across `full.jsonl` / `content_hash.txt` is the wrong move, and would actually break things.** Here's why, file by file:\n\n| File | What it actually is | Should ticket go here? |\n|------|--------------------|------------------------|\n| `metadata.json` | The sidecar for exactly this kind of structured provenance | ✅ **Already there** — correct home |\n| `full.jsonl` | The **raw, verbatim agent transcript**. CLI reads it byte-for-byte for rewind/resume/explain | ❌ Injecting ticket lines corrupts the real conversation record |\n| `transcript.jsonl` | Compact/redacted transcript *derived from* `full.jsonl` | ❌ Same corruption problem |\n| `content_hash.txt` | Literally `sha256(transcript bytes)`. Its only job is dedup — at `persistent.go:1830` the code compares old vs new hash to skip rewriting unchanged transcripts | ❌ It's a hash, not a container. Writing ticket text here **breaks dedup** |\n\nSo the ticket is already living in the one file that's *designed* to hold it (`metadata.json`). The other three each have a specific job, and the ticket doesn't belong in any of them — putting it there would corrupt transcripts or break the content-addressed dedup.\n\n**What I think you actually want** (from your last message — \"will I see it on my PR?\") isn't more files, it's *visibility*. The ticket is stored correctly; nothing reads it back out yet. The real work is on the read side:\n\n- surface it in `checkpoint explain` (so you see \"grounded in LIN-123: …\")\n- show it in `entire status`\n- feed it into `entire review` / the PR mirror\n\nWant me to add the **read/display** side instead? If so, which surface first — `checkpoint explain`, `entire status`, or the PR view? That's the piece that makes it show up when you check your PR.","type":"text"}]}
