eSessionInfoJSON` don't take `ctx` today, so resolve the link in `runSessionInfo` and pass it down.\n- Judgment: **genuinely useful.** It's a per-session detail view and branch is known; valuable especially for ended sessions inspected after the fact. Caveat: `state.Branch` is \"branch at last checkpoint\" and may be stale vs. the live link store, but that's acceptable for a detail view.\n\n### 2. `entire session list` — SKIP (noise)\n- Per-row renderer `writeSessionCard` at `sessions.go:415`; each `s` has `s.Branch`, so branch is available per row.\n- Plumbing: medium — a `LinkForBranch` lookup per row.\n- Judgment: **noise.** Tickets are branch-scoped, so multiple sessions on the same branch would repeat the same ticket line, bloating a compact one-card-per-session list. The list doesn't even print the branch today (it shows worktree, `sessions.go:427`). Skip.\n\n### 3. `entire session current` — SKIP (redundant + auto-covered)\n- `session_current.go:42` resolves `FindMostRecentSession` then delegates straight to `runSessionInfo` (`session_current.go:48`).\n- Overlap with `status`: **high** — it shows the active session for the current worktree, and `entire status` already prints the ticket for that worktree/branch (`status.go:196`).\n- Because it delegates to `runSessionInfo`, if you add the ticket to candidate #1 it **inherits it for free**. No separate work, and no reason to special-case it.\n\n### 4. `entire checkpoint list` — MARGINAL (header only; per-row is heavy)\n- `newCheckpointListCmd` (`checkpoint_group.go:55`) → `runExplainBranchWithFilter` (`explain.go:2411`).\n- Confirming the explorer: rows come from `[]strategy.RewindPoint` (`explain.go:2439`, `2729`). The `RewindPoint` struct (`strategy/strategy.go:46`) has **no `Ticket` field** — only `MetadataDir` (line 54). So per-row ticket data requires loading each checkpoint's `Metadata` from disk = **heavy plumbing and redundant** (and `checkpoint explain` already shows the frozen `meta.Ticket` per checkp